-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 42: DEBTORS ACT (part roc9, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- How to read a result: see the header of roc9-order-41.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING; never turn NOTHING into FALSE).
--
-- THE SHAPES THIS ORDER REPEATS.
-- * "X must be in Form N": one yes/no requirement.  The Form itself is not in this text, so whether the document is in that Form
--   is asked as a plain input.
-- * "must ..., unless the Court otherwise orders": two functions.  The companion `... applies` answers JUST FALSE when the exception
--   holds (the requirement does not apply); the compliance function then answers NOTHING (QD) and, when the requirement applies,
--   JUST TRUE if every limb is met and NOTHING if not (QB).
-- * The deposits of Rules 5 and 10 are due "before or at the end of" each period of 14 days: the last day of the period in question
--   is the seam input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` (Order 3, Rule 3 computes it; the part roc1 owns that rule).

